#### Testing System.String methods

There are numerous ways to test System.String methods, but in C# you could also use the Microsoft Fakes Framework. The test verifies that the method SystemBackslashToSlash correctly replaces all backslashes with slashes. 

```C#
[TestMethod]
public void SystemBackslashToSlashTest()
{
 using (ShimSystem shimSystem = new ShimSystem())
 {
 var expect = "c:\\p\\h\\a\\r\\d\\e\\r\\p\\a\\t\\h";
 // Act
 var actual = System.IO.Path.Combine("c:\\", "p", "h", "a", "r", "d", "e", "r", "p", "a", "t", "h");
 // Assert
 Assert.AreEqual(expect, actual);
 }
}

```

In this example, the shimSystem variable creates a shim class for the System.IO.Path which is then used to simulate the behavior of the System.IO.Path class methods. We replace the actual behavior of System.IO.Path.Combine (which we know does not work correctly for the purpose of this test) with a fake one. In this case, the fake method always returns the same string, regardless of the inputs. 

